Description: pvr: accept a NULL pCounterBuffers in transform feedback begin/end
 vkCmdBeginTransformFeedbackEXT and vkCmdEndTransformFeedbackEXT may be called
 with counterBufferCount > 0 and pCounterBuffers NULL, which means no counter
 buffers (vk.xml: pCounterBuffers is noautovalidity; radv, hasvk and hk check
 the pointer). pvr read pCounterBuffers[j] unconditionally and dereferenced
 NULL. dEQP-VK.transform_feedback.simple.resume_1_*_null_counter_buffers
 (NULL in begin) and resume_1_*_null_ptrs_end_xfb (NULL in end) end with a
 segmentation fault.
 .
 Treat a NULL array like VK_NULL_HANDLE entries: the binding gets no counter
 buffer address, as already done for single VK_NULL_HANDLE entries.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
